IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa2-ch4-other-powers.l4: Part 5, Chapter 4 (Other powers of the Secretary of State and the registrar) and Chapter 4A
-- (Exceptions), ss 75-76E, lines 877-982 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no point of view.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seams taken as inputs: s 1121 "officer in default" (coa24).  An opinion or satisfaction of the Secretary of State or
-- of the registrar is a plain input (TRUE: the opinion is held), never guessed.
-- The six directions to change a name (ss 64, 67, 75, 76, 76A, 76B) share a shape; s 76D(2) lists them in the Act's own words.
-- Every name that is not in coa-core.l4 begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Provision of misleading information (s 75)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 75(5) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 75(5) change the company's name as the direction requires`

-- src:879 | 75 Provision of misleading information etc
-- src:880 | (1) If it appears to the Secretary of State—
-- src:881 | (a) that misleading information has been given for the purposes of a company's registration by a particular name, or
-- src:882 | (b) that an undertaking or assurance has been given for that purpose and has not been fulfilled,
-- src:883 | the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name.
@ref s 75(1) Provision of misleading information etc (src:879-883)
GIVEN `it appears to the Secretary of State that misleading information has been given for the purposes of the company's registration by a particular name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that an undertaking or assurance has been given for that purpose and has not been fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(1) the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name` MEANS
    IF       `it appears to the Secretary of State that misleading information has been given for the purposes of the company's registration by a particular name`
         OR  `it appears to the Secretary of State that an undertaking or assurance has been given for that purpose and has not been fulfilled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the Secretary of State— (a) ... or (b) ..., the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name" (fork 14: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- src:879 | 75 Provision of misleading information etc
-- src:884 | (2) Any such direction—
-- src:885 | (a) must be given within five years of the company's registration by that name, and
@ref s 75(2)(a) A direction must be given within five years of the registration (src:879-885)
GIVEN `the date of the company's registration by that name` IS A DATE
      `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(2)(a) the direction is given within five years of the company's registration by that name` MEANS
    IF `the date of the direction` AT MOST (`add years` `the date of the company's registration by that name` 5)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- five years of the registration: up to and including the same date five years later (fork 3)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given within five years of the company's registration by that name"

-- src:884 | (2) Any such direction—
-- src:886 | (b) must specify the period within which the company is to change its name.
@ref s 75(2)(b) A direction must specify the period (src:884-886)
GIVEN `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(2)(b) the direction specifies the period` MEANS
    IF `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must specify the period within which the company is to change its name"

-- src:887 | (2A) The period must be at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction.
@ref s 75(2A) The period: at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction (src:887-887)
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(2A) the period meets the requirement of subsection (2A)` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period` AT LEAST (`the date of the direction` PLUS 27)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the period beginning with the date of the direction and ending on that day is at least 28 days
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period must be at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction"

-- src:888 | (3) The Secretary of State may by a further direction extend the period within which the company is to change its name.
-- src:889 | Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified.
@ref s 75(3) Further direction extending the period (src:888-889)
GIVEN `the date of the further direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period for the time being specified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(3) the Secretary of State may give a further direction extending the period` MEANS
    IF `the date of the further direction` AT MOST `the last day of the period for the time being specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- fork 2: a direction given on the last day is given before the end of the period
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified"

-- src:890 | (4) A direction under this section must be in writing.
@ref s 75(4) A direction under this section must be in writing (src:890-890)
GIVEN `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(4) the direction meets the requirement of being in writing` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A direction under this section must be in writing"

-- src:891 | (4A) Where a direction is given under subsection (1), the registrar may omit from the material on the register that is available for public inspection any mention of the name to which the direction relates.
@ref s 75(4A) Registrar may omit the name from the public register (src:891-891)
GIVEN `a direction is given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(4A) the registrar may omit from the register material available for public inspection any mention of the name to which the direction relates` MEANS
    IF `a direction is given under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a direction is given under subsection (1), the registrar may omit"

-- src:892 | (5) If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:893 | (a) the company, and
-- src:894 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 75(5) Failure to comply with a direction (the duty and its time limit) (src:892-894)
GIVEN `days allowed by the direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 75(5) act`
`s 75(5) the company's duty to change its name as directed` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 75(5) change the company's name as the direction requires`
    WITHIN `days allowed by the direction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company failed to comply with the direction: an offence is committed under section 75(5)"

-- src:892 | (5) If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:893 | (a) the company, and
-- src:894 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:895 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 75(5) Failure to comply with a direction (who commits the offence) (src:892-895)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with a direction under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company fails to comply with a direction under this section`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `Officer in default` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Director THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Company secretary` THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Shadow director` THEN `liability of an officer` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company."
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; it does not say that no one else commits the offence
    WHERE
        `liability of an officer` MEANS
            IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:896 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 75(6) Offence (penalty) (src:896-896)
`s 75(6) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

