-- src:929 | (11) If a company fails to comply with a direction under subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:930 | (a) the company, and
-- src:931 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 76A(11) Failure to comply with a direction (the duty and its time limit) (src:929-931)
GIVEN `days allowed by the direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76A(11) act`
`s 76A(11) the company's duty to change its name as directed` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 76A(11) change the company's name as the direction requires`
    WITHIN `days allowed by the direction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company failed to comply with the direction: an offence is committed under section 76A(11)"

-- src:929 | (11) If a company fails to comply with a direction under subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:930 | (a) the company, and
-- src:931 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:932 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 76A(11) Failure to comply with a direction (who commits the offence) (src:929-932)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with a direction under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(11) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company fails to comply with a direction under subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with a direction under subsection (1), an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `Officer in default` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Director THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Company secretary` THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Shadow director` THEN `liability of an officer` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company."
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; it does not say that no one else commits the offence
    WHERE
        `liability of an officer` MEANS
            IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:933 | (12) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 76A(12) Offence (penalty) (src:933-933)
`s 76A(12) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

