DECLARE `s 76B(11) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76B(11) change the company's name as the direction requires`

-- src:934 | Direction to change name wrongly registered
-- src:935 | 76B Direction to change name wrongly registered
-- src:936 | (1) The Secretary of State may direct a company to change its name if—
-- src:937 | (a) it appears to the Secretary of State that the company’s registration by that name was in contravention of any requirement imposed by this Part, or
-- src:938 | (b) the Secretary of State did not, at the time at which the name was registered, form the opinion mentioned in section 53, 56A or 57A, but had proper grounds for doing so.
@ref s 76B(1) Direction to change name wrongly registered (src:934-938)
GIVEN `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company's registration by that name was in contravention of any requirement imposed by Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State did not, at the time at which the name was registered, form the opinion mentioned in section 53, 56A or 57A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming that opinion at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(1) the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name` MEANS
    IF       `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company's registration by that name was in contravention of any requirement imposed by Part 5`
         OR  (    `the Secretary of State did not, at the time at which the name was registered, form the opinion mentioned in section 53, 56A or 57A`
              AND `the Secretary of State had proper grounds for forming that opinion at that time`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may direct a company to change its name if— (a) ... or (b) ..." (fork 17: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- src:935 | 76B Direction to change name wrongly registered
-- src:939 | (2) The direction must be in writing and must specify the period within which the company is to change its name.
@ref s 76B(2) The direction: in writing, specifying the period (src:935-939)
GIVEN `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(2) the direction meets the requirements of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing` AND `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The direction must be in writing and must specify the period within which the company is to change its name"

-- src:935 | 76B Direction to change name wrongly registered
-- src:940 | (3) The period must be a period of at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction.
@ref s 76B(3) The period: at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction (src:935-940)
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(3) the period meets the requirement of subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period` AT LEAST (`the date of the direction` PLUS 27)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the period beginning with the date of the direction and ending on that day is at least 28 days
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period must be a period of at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction"

-- src:935 | 76B Direction to change name wrongly registered
-- src:941 | (4) The Secretary of State may by further direction in writing extend the period.
-- src:942 | Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified.
@ref s 76B(4) Further direction in writing extending the period (src:935-942)
GIVEN `the further direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the further direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period for the time being specified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(4) the Secretary of State may give a further direction extending the period` MEANS
    IF `the date of the further direction` AT MOST `the last day of the period for the time being specified`
    THEN IF `the further direction is in writing`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- fork 2: a direction given on the last day is given before the end of the period
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by further direction in writing" (fork 21: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified"

