-- =========================================================================================================
-- Exceptions (s 76E, Chapter 4A)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:976 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:977 | (a) “crime” means conduct which—
-- src:978 | (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or
-- src:979 | (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence, and
@ref s 76E(2)(a) "crime" (src:976-979)
GIVEN `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is, or corresponds to, conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(2)(a) the conduct is crime` MEANS
    IF       `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence`
         OR  `the conduct is, or corresponds to, conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“crime” means conduct which— (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence"

-- src:976 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:980 | (b) crime is “serious” if—
-- src:981 | (i) the offence which is or would be constituted by the conduct is an offence for which the maximum sentence (in any part of the United Kingdom) is imprisonment for 3 years or more, or
-- src:982 | (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose.
@ref s 76E(2)(b) "serious" (src:976-982)
GIVEN `the greatest maximum term of imprisonment, in years, for the offence in any part of the United Kingdom` IS A NUMBER
      `the conduct involves the use of violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct results in substantial financial gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(2)(b) the crime is serious` MEANS
    IF       `the greatest maximum term of imprisonment, in years, for the offence in any part of the United Kingdom` AT LEAST 3
         OR  `the conduct involves the use of violence`
         OR  `the conduct results in substantial financial gain`
         OR  `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "crime is “serious” if— (i) ... imprisonment for 3 years or more, or (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose"

-- src:972 | 76E Exceptions based on national security etc
-- src:973 | (1) Nothing in this Part prevents the registration of a company under this Act by a name if the Secretary of State is satisfied that the registration of the company by that name is necessary—
-- src:974 | (a) in the interests of national security, or
-- src:975 | (b) for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime.
@ref s 76E(1) Exceptions based on national security etc (src:972-975)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the registration of the company by that name is necessary in the interests of national security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the registration of the company by that name is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting the crime in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the crime in question is serious crime (s 76E(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(1) Part 5 does not prevent the registration of the company by the name` MEANS
    IF       `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the registration of the company by that name is necessary in the interests of national security`
         OR  (    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the registration of the company by that name is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting the crime in question`
              AND `the crime in question is serious crime (s 76E(2))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text says so: "Nothing in this Part prevents the registration of a company under this Act by a name if the Secretary of State is satisfied"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this Part prevents the registration ... if the Secretary of State is satisfied that the registration ... is necessary" in (a) or (b)
